# Citation metadata for the site and its computed datasets.
# GENERATED FIELDS: version and date-released mirror data/version.json;
# scripts/check-citation.mjs fails CI when they drift. Everything else is
# hand-maintained. See also data/citations.bib (generated BibTeX for the
# site, its export tables, and all 25 cited sources).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this site or its computed datasets, please cite it as below.
  Bundled upstream data keeps its own licenses and should be cited
  separately; see NOTICE.md and https://divinediscourses.org/sources.
title: "Divine Discourses"
type: software
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-09
url: "https://divinediscourses.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/saebchicago/qurandiscourses"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "Divine Discourses project"
    website: "https://divinediscourses.org/about"
abstract: >-
  A Qur'an study platform in the coherence-reading tradition of
  Dr. Irfan Ahmad Khan: each surah read as one discourse, every claim
  labeled and traceable to its source. Ships word-by-word morphology
  (Leeds Quranic Arabic Corpus v0.4), computed root, association,
  centrality, and coverage datasets, and a machine-readable claims
  ledger with per-claim evidence status.
keywords:
  - Quran
  - Arabic morphology
  - corpus linguistics
  - coherence
  - nazm
references:
  - type: data
    title: "The Quranic Arabic Corpus, version 0.4"
    authors:
      - family-names: Dukes
        given-names: Kais
    url: "https://corpus.quran.com"
    notes: "GPL; the morphology foundation for all computed datasets."
